  "goodToKnow": "Die Kehle is the throat: eine trockene Kehle haben. In everyday speech, Germans more often say der Hals. Kehle appears in vivid idioms: aus voller Kehle singen (to sing at the top of your voice), etwas in die falsche Kehle bekommen (to take something the wrong way, literally down the wrong throat), and das Messer an der Kehle haben (to have a knife at your throat, to be under pressure). Der Kehlkopf is the larynx."
